{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-core":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-core/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-quantum-gauge-group-category","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:quantum-gauge-group-category","kind":"remark","title":"Quantum gauge group: category-theoretic perspective","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-quantum-gauge-group"],"interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-quantum-gauge-group","tags":["tannaka-krein","hopf-algebra","category-theory"],"text":"quantum-gauge-group-category.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"rem:quantum-gauge-group-category\"></a><p>The quantum gauge group operates fibrewise via the representation category <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{Rep}(\\mathrm{SU}_{q(p)}(2))</code>. Tannaka--Krein duality reconstructs the Hopf algebra <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{O}_{q(p)}(\\mathrm{SU}(2))</code> through the forgetful fibre functor. The Hopf-algebra and representation-category viewpoints are equivalent across fibres.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-gauge-group-category.md","heading":"Remark","number":"4.26.3","page":"b/rem-quantum-gauge-group-category","qa":{"counts":{"pass":57,"fail":2,"warn":0,"na":18,"unknown":0,"stale":50},"milnor":{"total":2,"notPassing":1}}}
